  "body": "# Bookokrat 0.3.13\r\n\r\n## Highlights\r\n\r\n- Added reading from stdin (`curl … | bookokrat -`); piped documents resume with their highlights and comments.\r\n- Added a `--no-images` text-only mode.\r\n- Inline annotation bodies can be hidden with `Space+i` and peeked at with `K` / `Space+k`.\r\n\r\n## Improvements\r\n\r\n- Large libraries no longer slow down startup; the library is scanned in the background.\r\n- EPUB images now fit the reader view; the old fixed size is available in settings.\r\n- Smoother image scrolling in iTerm2, WezTerm, Konsole and Warp.\r\n- Added Android (Termux) support.\r\n\r\n## Fixes\r\n\r\n- Dialogue lines that start with a dash are no longer merged into a single paragraph.\r\n- Highlights and comments after a line break no longer land a few characters early.\r\n- PDF zoom, zen mode, enhance and dual-page switching keep the reading position; fixed dual-page loading hangs.\r\n- Fixed text selection in multi-column PDFs.\r\n- PDF pages no longer linger after switching tmux windows in newer Ghostty versions.\r\n- Fixed keyboard input when stdin is redirected, `Ctrl+o` after following links, and the page-scroll highlight at document edges.\r\n- Improved Nord theme status-line readability.\r\n- Fixed builds on FreeBSD and with the Nix flake.\r\n\r\n## Upgrade notes\r\n\r\n- Annotations, positions and marks are migrated to the new dialogue layout on first open; older versions will show them misplaced.\r\n- PDF normal mode: `a` now adds a comment (was `d`), `dd` deletes it.\r\n"
